{
  "id": "b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices",
  "level": "B2",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Climate and everyday choices",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good afternoon. First of all, we'd like to know something about you.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4600
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what do you like about the place where you live?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4000
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, how do you usually get around your town?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3900
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what do you do at home that is good for the environment?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4800
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, how much do you worry about climate change?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you two photographs. I'd like you to talk about them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question about your partner's photographs.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e07-a1",
            "b2-e07-a2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your photographs show people travelling around a city. Compare the photographs, and say what the people might like and dislike about travelling in these ways.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 11400
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, which of these would you prefer? Why?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4000
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "b2-e07-b1",
            "b2-e07-b2"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your photographs show people taking care of the environment. Compare the photographs, and say why the people might have decided to do this.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 10400
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, do you think it is easy to live in a way that is good for the environment? Why or why not?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some things that can help people reduce their effect on the environment, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 11900
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these things help people look after the environment?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6800
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which would make the biggest difference?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about the environment and climate.",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Some people say that individuals can do very little to stop climate change. Do you agree?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6300
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, should governments force people to change their habits?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think young people care more about the environment than older people?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6000
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Is it fair to ask poorer countries to protect the environment in the same way as richer ones?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6800
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, what do you think is the most important change your town could make?",
          "audio": "audio/B2/b2-e07-climate-and-everyday-choices/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5800
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
